# LFS is OFF, deliberately and unambiguously.
#
# This file used to carry BOTH `*.zip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text` and
# `*.zip !text !filter !merge !diff` (same for *.gif). Attributes resolve
# last-match-wins per attribute, so the second pair already cleared filter,
# merge and diff -- LFS was inert while the file read as if it were enabled.
# The enabling lines are removed rather than the clearing ones, so the file now
# says what git was already doing.
#
# Why off rather than on: no .zip or .gif is tracked in this repository, and an
# LFS-enabled repo hands plain-git clones pointer stubs instead of content --
# a failure preflight_cpu.sh has to check for by name ("truncated or an LFS
# pointer stub"). Nothing here is worth that.
#
# The consequence to keep in mind: with LFS off, any large binary that escapes
# .gitignore enters git as a plain blob, permanently. The PARSeq checkpoint is
# ~286 MB and lives in plugins/jn_gsr/models/, which .gitignore excludes. Do
# not add checkpoints anywhere else, and do not un-ignore that directory.
*.zip !text !filter !merge !diff
*.gif !text !filter !merge !diff

# Shell scripts run on Linux (Lightning AI) — always store/check out with LF endings
*.sh text eol=lf
